From 9aaa82f27c0202459dcc285d029f95ea6bd768b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 20:28:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08555/11362] fix: preserve freshness-lint acknowledgements
 across analyser rebuilds

ops/known-issues.md's "related, systemic defect" entry: every analyser script
built art["provenance"] = {...} wholesale and overwrote its output JSON --
including the exact path the freshness lint's own "rebuild with: ..." remedy
points a reader at -- silently destroying any provenance.freshness_acknowledgements
the file already carried. Self-concealing: the rebuild also refreshes
provenance.code[*].sha256, so the lint goes GREEN at the exact moment the
audit trail is erased. 170 acknowledgement blocks were exposed across 13 of
16 tracked artifacts at the time this was filed.

Shared helper preserve_freshness_acknowledgements(art, out_path) added to
scripts/analyze_scored_path_lever_ab.py (already imported by all 16 analysers
for register_analyzed_artifact): reads whatever's on disk at out_path before
the overwrite and copies forward ONLY freshness_acknowledgements -- every
other provenance field still refreshes correctly on rebuild, since only the
acknowledgement log is an append-only audit trail rather than a fact about
the current build.

Wired into all 16 analysers' write site(s) via an adversarially-verified
fan-out (15 wire agents + 15 independent re-verification agents, each
re-running the dry-run itself). 2 files had 2 write sites (a normal-completion
path and a precondition-blocked early-exit path); both wired in each case.
13/15 CONFIRMED outright by independent re-verification, 2/15
PARTIALLY_CONFIRMED (wording inaccuracies in the wiring agent's own
self-report only -- both re-verified working code, no rework needed).

This commit carries 15 of 16 wired files; the helper itself and its unit
tests already landed (correct, but under an unrelated commit message -- see
the "One honest provenance note" this commit adds to known-issues.md,
commits a9d4b13922 / 7303588b67, swept in by the conductor's own git add -A
while this fix was mid-edit).

Also includes: freshness-lint acknowledgements on all 16 affected artifacts
(each analyser's own hash changed) plus one second-order cascade
(outer_loop_arc_gateway_accurate_rescore_20260726.json cites two of those 16
artifacts by content hash). Every acknowledgement reasons that the wiring
diff is provably inert for the artifact's OWN numbers: the helper only takes
effect on a FUTURE rebuild of the same output path.

Tests: tests/python/test_analyze_scored_path_lever_ab.py::
TestPreserveFreshnessAcknowledgements (7 tests, already landed). Verified per
file: ruff/ruff-format/ast.parse clean on all 16 changed files; a real
scratch dry-run per analyser (never touching the real tracked artifact)
confirmed acknowledgements survive a rebuild while every other provenance
field refreshes. Freshness-lint clean (exit 0) after acknowledgements.

